1f3af263 [gpt-5.3-codex] #• Common “std” approaches:*
1f3af264 [gpt-5.3-codex] #
1f3af264 [gpt-5.3-codex] #1. `std::ostringstream`
1f3af264 [gpt-5.3-codex] #	- Most traditional and clear.
1f3af264 [gpt-5.3-codex] #	- Loop through strings, stream each one in, optionally add delimiter.
1f3af265 [gpt-5.3-codex] #	- Get final text with `.str()`.
1f3af265 [gpt-5.3-codex] #
1f3af265 [gpt-5.3-codex] #2. `std::accumulate` (from `<numeric>`)
1f3af265 [gpt-5.3-codex] #	- Functional style reduction over the vector.
1f3af266 [gpt-5.3-codex] #	- Works, but often less readable and can create extra temporary strings.
1f3af266 [gpt-5.3-codex] #	- Fine for small/medium data.
1f3af266 [gpt-5.3-codex] #
